Hmm. Perhaps you haven't seen how much code is necessary to do this
"right". See
  http://vt100.net/emu/dec_ansi_parser
for a state transition diagram (and a link to source code - farther
down) of the ANSI sequences as implemented by DEC in their terminals.
xterm implements almost the exact same state transitions (I looked at
adapting xterm at one point - lots of code...). Interhack (as
described in other responses) appears to implement a sufficient subset
(it may be complete - I haven't checked). My main point was to mention
the shortcut of using a simpler TERM definition to reduce the code
needed to get past this step.

