That last alternative (canning the introduction) is certainly a good
simplification. A shortcut I considered was judicious use of control-L
(to refresh the screen) during debugging to aid in analysis of the
flow of data going to the screen. Another idea was to transparently
use far look "under the hood" to gain information automatically about
items that may appear the same on the screen but are different in
nethack.

